Ascension of a Healer

I am in the process of ascending all NetHack's roles in alphabetical
order and this time it's Healer. It took me full five weeks to ascend
one and all summed it was so far the hardest role. My attempts
included endless row of YASD, most of them were choking on food after
eating large chunk of meat. There was also one spectacular failure
less than hunderd turns before ascending, where Death killed my souped-
up Healer, who forgot to don his CoMR when setting off to ascension
run in VoTD.

Fourteen games were required after this to win. The game was mostly
defined by what it lacked. Many items I take for granted were never
found in it. So I never found following items:
- magic lamp
- wand of polymorph
- tinning kit
- ring of teleport control (I wished for it in the end)
- ring of conflict (I wish for it too)
- ring of free action
- wand of cancellation
I also never got anything from throne except mapping in Vlad's Tower
(where it is so useful!)

As a gnome, I went directly to the Mines, where in Minetown there were
bones with empty, but cursed, bag of holding. I never used it, as I
found uncursed one in Lower Mines. The temple was coaligned and when I
got to sacrifice, I got Magicbane on second attempt.

In Sokoban I, luckily, got amulet of reflection, so I had reflection
and MR, which is nice to have this early. I also had early ring of
levitation, speed boots and robe.

I found Fort Ludios entrance on a level with temple, so I cleared it.
At this point serious SNAFU happened -- my game crashed and I couldn't
restore it. Fortunately, paxed could, but to state before I cleared
FL, so I had to do that once again.

Medusa and Castle were unremarkable and after establishing my stash in
VoTD, I embarked on my Quest. All went nicely until I got to Cyclops,
where I got very very close call. Despite being very fast, in a single
turn he got me from over 100 HP down to 10 HP while also level
draining me. Were I little less lucky, the game would end at this
point. Anyway, I took no risks, engraved Elbereth and zapped him with
wand of death.

After processing loot in VoTD, I noted message on #nethack about a
well kitted wizard who died on Juiblex's level. I quick dived to
Gehennom in attempt to get his bones, but to no avail. At any rate, I
extensively mapped Gehennom in the hope of getting some of the missing
pieces of equipment. I did picture perfect Orcus kill, thus getting
his fully charged wand of death. When I arrived on a level before VS
level, master lich teleported to me and immediately summoned
Demogorgon. I was really scared as I was blindfolded and burdened, but
I managed to engrave Elbereth before he could hurt me, and after that
he was quickly defeated (my first Demo kill ever). During the Gehennom
I had two run ins with mind flayers, so I needed to remap some levels.
I also had to return to Minetown for missing candles and made a stop
to Sokoban, where I used my found cursed scroll of genocide to
revgenocide nurses. This did not net me that much hitpoints as I hoped
for. Single nurse on Medusa once gave me better HP increase. After
final session in VoTD (alchemizing potions, wishing for remaining
items) I started ascension run, which was rather nominal. In Moloch's
Sanctum Rodney appeared and quickly teleported to the high priest of
Moloch and they were exchanging punches while I waited for Rodney to
win and return to me with the Amulet. But then I was informed on
#nethack that this is unlikely to happen, so I had to go to retrieve
the Amulet myself. At least, I could kill the high priest and Rodney
with single zap of wand of death. Then I quaffed my precious
alchemized cursed potion of gain level and started running for the
Planes. On the way, Rodney was pestering me often and once I had to
kill him twice, since he was wearing amulet of life saving! The Planes
were completely nominal. On Astral Plane I lit the Candelabrum and
used jumping spell and wand of teleportation to quickly move about. I
was unlucky, only the third altar was the right one. BTW, I once had
Death killed by some priest for me. How nice.

In summary, I feel that Healer is the real challenge role of NetHack.
Really weak in the beginning, unable to wear heavy armor without
hurting his spellcasting, restricted in all but one school of magic.
Healer's reliance on pets also means acquiring intrinsics isn't very
easy. Later this levels up and with his superior quest artifact things
start to be much easier. On higher levels he can even cast level 3
spells reliably (useful for identify).

Next role is Knight.

